# GDExtension adapter

Canonical guidance: `docs/engineering/gdextension.md`. Version policy: `docs/engineering/VERSIONS.md`. Runtime boundary: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

Keep the adapter thin: Godot-facing values -> protocol -> authoritative core -> result/projection/events -> Godot-facing values.

Godot Engine, API target and godot-cpp revision are separate version dimensions. Never write `godot-cpp 4.7.x`; use the exact immutable v10 revision from active build/lock configuration and the policy in `VERSIONS.md`.

Do not:
- export mutable `World*` or internal object graphs;
- put trade/spell/world laws in `GDCLASS` methods;
- include godot-cpp from `src/sim` or `src/protocol`;
- throw ordinary gameplay outcomes across the boundary;
- add a second SCons project build graph;
- depend on floating godot-cpp branches.

A binding change is not verified until native tests, adapter build, Godot load and the relevant round-trip check actually run.
